# Kernel verdict

Import Conventions from "./conventions.lg".
Import KernelReport from "./kernel_report.lg".
Import NodeRecord from "./node_record.lg".
Import VerdictRecord from "./verdict_record.lg".

The acceptance policy, applied to one kernel run. It is fixed, and no agent can
edit it: every block checked; the closing `Check <proof>.` printed exactly
`<proof> : <goal>`; the closing `Print Axioms <proof>.` reports a closure inside
`propext`, `Quot_sound` and `Classical_choice`; and, before any of that, the
submission's reading and its name probes let it through. `largo` exits 0 exactly
when the document checked and 1 when a block was refused, so a run whose exit
disagrees with its own report is infrastructure, never a verdict.

## To kernelVerdict (exitCode: Int, stdout: Text, timedOut: Bool, proofName: Text, goalName: Text) -> Verdict:
    If timedOut:
        Return infrastructureVerdict("largo ran past its deadline").
    Inspect parseKernelReport(stdout):
        When Err (e):
            Return infrastructureVerdict("largo exited {exitCode}; " + e).
        When Ok (report):
            Let exitedClean be exitCode is equal to 0.
            If report's checked is not equal to exitedClean or exitCode is greater than 1:
                Return infrastructureVerdict("the report and largo's exit status {exitCode} disagree").
            If report's checked is equal to false:
                Return newVerdict("rejected", report's failedBlock, report's error, [], "the kernel refused the document").
            Return closingVerdict(report's outputs, proofName, goalName).
    Return infrastructureVerdict("unreadable run").

## Note
The verdict the closing checks give, read off the last two block outputs.

## To closingVerdict (outputs: Seq of Text, proofName: Text, goalName: Text) -> Verdict:
    Let n be length of outputs.
    If n is less than 2:
        Return newVerdict("rejected", n, "the document has no closing checks", [], "the factory's closing checks did not run as written").
    If item (n - 1) of outputs is not equal to proofName + " : " + goalName:
        Return newVerdict("rejected", n - 1, "`Check {proofName}.` printed `{item (n - 1) of outputs}`, not `{proofName} : {goalName}`", [], "the proof does not have the goal as its type").
    Inspect axiomsOf(item n of outputs, proofName):
        When Err (e):
            Return newVerdict("rejected", n, e, [], "the factory's closing checks did not run as written").
        When Ok (axioms):
            Let outside be disallowedAxioms(axioms).
            If length of outside is equal to 0:
                Return newVerdict("verified", 0, "", axioms, "every block checked; the proof rests on " + axiomPhrase(axioms) + ", within propext, Quot_sound and Classical_choice").
            Return newVerdict("admitted_axiom", 0, "", axioms, "every block checked, but the proof rests on " + join(outside, ", ") + ", outside propext, Quot_sound and Classical_choice").
    Return infrastructureVerdict("unreadable closing checks").

## Note
The verdict name probes add, or `none` when every declared name was free; `what`
is the document probed and `boundBy` what it was probed against.

## To nameProbeVerdict (what: Text, boundBy: Text, names: Seq of Text, outcomes: Seq of Text) -> Option of Verdict:
    Repeat for i from 1 to length of names:
        If item i of outcomes is equal to "bound":
            Return some newVerdict("rejected", 0, "the {what} declares {item i of names}, which {boundBy} already binds", [], "a {what} may only add new names").
    Repeat for i from 1 to length of names:
        If item i of outcomes is not equal to "free":
            Return some infrastructureVerdict("the probe of {item i of names} did not answer").
    Return none.

## Note
Whether a proof document is bound to an accepted statement: the statement hashes
to its recorded hash and the document begins with it as the assembler places it.

## To boundToStatement (statement: Statement, document: Text) -> Bool:
    If sha256Hex(statement's document) is not equal to statement's sha256:
        Return false.
    Return startsWith(document, trimEnd(statement's document) + "\n\n/-! ## Submission -/\n\n").
